WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.360
"How Much Do Doctors Know About Nutrition?"

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.480
Humanity's diet is the single
leading cause of death,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.160
exacting an even greater
health burden than smoking.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.920
This makes sense
since we are what we eat.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.640
Literally, physically.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.120
If we continue to rebuild
our body every day

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.400
with shoddy materials,

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.720
it's no wonder
we run into trouble.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.040
For example, not eating enough
fruits and vegetables

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.960
is blamed for millions
of deaths every year.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.120
We should eat fruits
and vegetables

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.280
as if our lives depended on it,

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.680
because in a way,
it appears they do.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.000
Most Americans may be suffering
from diet-related diseases,

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.440
yet most are not being educated
about nutrition

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.320
from their doctors.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.280
Maybe that's
actually a good thing

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.320
given how little doctors
tend to know about nutrition?

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.520
Physicians are typically seen

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.840
as trustworthy sources
of nutrition

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.400
by the general public,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.920
but in a head-to-head test
of nutrition knowledge,

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.760
doctors versus patients,

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.360
though physicians
should be more knowledgeable

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:04.120
about nutrition
than their patients,

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.640
these results suggest that
this is not necessarily true.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.520
And we all know how little
the general public knows

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:11.960
about nutrition.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.880
The American diet is
the number one cause of death

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.840
in the United States,
yet doctors average

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.160
less than 20 hours
of nutrition training

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:20.320
and that's mostly
like, you know,

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.120
biochemistry of vitamins.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.560
The amount of clinical
nutrition training they may get

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.880
is less than five hours.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.000
Take cardiology, for example.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.320
Dr. Ornish's landmark
lifestyle heart trial

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.760
asked the question:
"Can lifestyle changes reverse

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.120
coronary artery disease?"

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.600
And the answer
was a resounding yes.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.360
If just that tidbit alone
were understood

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.600
and internalized by internists,

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.520
think how many lives
could be saved

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.840
from our leading cause
of death and disability,

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.480
yet 90 percent
of surveyed cardiologists

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.720
reported receiving little
or no nutrition education

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.920
during their
cardiology training.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.160
There appears to be
insufficient nutrition training

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.840
in medical training
across the board,

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.920
a global deficiency.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.880
The low hanging fruit
in medicine

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:06.600
remains on the vine.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.520
And for those doctors who say
they don't have time,

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:12.360
physicians don't need to do
their own diet counseling

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.760
any more than
they need to perform

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.160
their own x-rays
or blood draws.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.760
But they must
recognize the role

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.280
nutrition plays in disease,

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.240
communicate it clearly
to patients,

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.320
and refer the patient
appropriately.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.160
The diet that Dr. Ornish used
to help reverse

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.800
the progression
of heart disease

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.200
was whole-food,
plant-based nutrition,

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.280
a diet primarily,
but not exclusively,

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.200
composed of fruits, vegetables,
whole grains, and legumes.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.080
Why isn't there
more widespread acknowledgement

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:42.000
of the power of plants
in the medical community?

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.760
One potential reason
is that the science

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.040
has yet to make its way
into the teaching materials.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.560
Yes, Dr. Ornish made
this discovery decades ago,

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.480
but, sometimes,
it can take decades

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.080
for medical practice
to catch up,

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.360
even when millions of lives
are at stake.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.840
Nowadays,
it would be unthinkable

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.360
not to address
patients' smoking,

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.720
because it's just been
incorporated

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.280
into the standard of care.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.240
The evidence on nutrition has
yet to be similarly lionized,

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.480
but "[t]his should not prevent

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.200
thoughtful
and caring clinicians

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.600
from applying
safe and effective

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:14.800
nutritional interventions

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:17.080
that are not
'ahead of the evidence'

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.920
but only ahead
of the [published] guidelines."

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.640
Ignorance of nutrition
is no longer defensible.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.720
There are a growing number
of resources

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.480
for those who missed out
in med school.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.960
Doctors can get board certified
in lifestyle medicine.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.920
There are some great websites
out there.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:37.080
Like PCRM's "Nutrition Guide
for Clinicians."

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.840
More great websites.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.040
Yes, it would be nice
not to be a hypocrite

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.720
and eat more
healthfully yourself

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.880
rather than just learning
about healthier diets,

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.680
but that shouldn't stop anyone
from recommending it,

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:51.000
if only because it is
the only diet

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.880
that has ever been shown
to reverse the progression

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.520
of the number one killer
of men and women,

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.840
so people should not be denied
such knowledge.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.360
Now, look, it's their body,
their choice.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:03.120
Just like many smokers
will continue to smoke,

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.360
many will continue to eat junk,

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.920
but this should not prevent
clinicians from advising

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:11.120
smoking cessation
and a healthier diet.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.720
Patients have the right
to be told the truth.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.080
Not mentioning
this powerful dietary tool

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.360
is an act of withholding
crucial information

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.920
necessary
for fully informed consent.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.120
Unfortunately,
out of ignorance,

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:26.880
what many doctors are telling
their patients to eat

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.760
may be killing them.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.280
Some doctors used to smoke
with their patients.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.480
In fact, most doctors
themselves smoked,

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.080
just like most doctors today
continue to eat foods

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.840
that are contributing
to our epidemics

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.360
in dietary disease.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:43.280
Until doctors are taught more
about nutrition,

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.680
their advising people
about their diet

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.969
could be considered a form
of physician-assisted suicide.

